WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.950
- We need to talk about the
new season of Magnum P.I.

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:05.160
So what can you tell us about
what's happening right now?

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.740
- The new season is a lot of the same.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.840
There's a lot of action, a lot of fun.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.320
There's this very strong
family sort of quality

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.480
to all the characters on the show.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:16.313
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:16.313 --> 00:00:19.230
- So, I mean, it's kind of
all the stuff that we expect,

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.840
but I also direct an episode.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:22.673
- Oh, is that something

00:00:22.673 --> 00:00:23.550
you're interested in doing?
- I directed one last-

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:24.510
I love it.
- Oh, that's cool.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:25.343
- I love it.

00:00:25.343 --> 00:00:27.690
It's this really kind of interesting thing

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:30.300
where as an actor, Jay
Hernandez, the individual,

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.250
has to kind of stay in his lane,

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:35.010
but as a director you
can kind of go outside

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:36.570
and play outside the
boundaries a little bit.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:37.403
So that's one

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:38.636
thing that I love about it
- It's interesting 'cause

00:00:38.636 --> 00:00:39.720
I've never had any
interest like behind that.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.390
Like I've just never, it's
just never pulled at me.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:43.223
- Mm-hmm.

00:00:43.223 --> 00:00:44.056
- And it's interesting, like,

00:00:44.056 --> 00:00:45.420
I feel like it's actors
a lot of times too.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.580
Like, y'all (indistinct) musicians,

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.500
it's like actors really like to be a part

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.600
of the whole story, not
just their one characters.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:52.633
I find that a lot on the couch.

00:00:52.633 --> 00:00:53.760
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:55.080
I think what it is, is like,

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:57.660
there's just a type of freedom
that you have as a director

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.090
that you don't necessarily
have as an actor.

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:00.923
- Yeah.

00:01:00.923 --> 00:01:02.400
- Because, you know, you're
just not afforded the liberty

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.984
to play a a million different
characters sometimes.

00:01:04.984 --> 00:01:05.817
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:05.817 --> 00:01:06.990
- You know, like whatever they think I am,

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:08.820
it's like I gotta kind
of stay in that lane.

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:10.740
- [Kelly] I hate that when
people get typecasted.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:11.610
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:12.720
- What's the craziest stunt though?

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.520
Cuz it's action packed, So like what's-

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:15.353
- [Jay] There's a lot of action.

00:01:15.353 --> 00:01:16.186
- Do you like the action?

00:01:16.186 --> 00:01:17.019
Doing all that?
- I love it. I love it.

00:01:17.019 --> 00:01:17.852
- Okay.

00:01:17.852 --> 00:01:19.410
- Yeah. I absolutely love it.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:22.320
I don't love it when I have,
you got two-pound burrito

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:23.346
and then gotta' sprint on top of a rooftop

00:01:23.346 --> 00:01:24.240
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:25.073
or something like that.

00:01:25.073 --> 00:01:25.930
- Yeah.

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:26.763
- Don't love that.

00:01:26.763 --> 00:01:30.445
But I've done everything on the
show, car stunts, like guns,

00:01:30.445 --> 00:01:33.270
like chasing people, fight
scenes, all this stuff.

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:34.530
But one of the coolest things

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:37.714
was in the episode I directed last season.

00:01:37.714 --> 00:01:38.547
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:38.547 --> 00:01:40.050
- I was, we were doing
this underwater stuff

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:42.390
and it was just like this easy shot of me,

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:44.100
kind of like floating through the ocean

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:47.280
looking for some sunken vessel and-

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:48.113
- [Kelly] That's cool.

00:01:48.113 --> 00:01:49.440
- And well, that's not
the coolest part about it.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:50.273
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:01:50.273 --> 00:01:51.521
- So I'm like probably 60-feet

00:01:51.521 --> 00:01:53.550
under the surface of the ocean.

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:55.920
And the coordinator stunt guy,

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.110
he tells me to turn
around and I turn around,

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:01.230
and there was a pod of like 60 dolphins

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:02.063
that were-

00:02:02.063 --> 00:02:02.896
- [Derek] Amazing.

00:02:02.896 --> 00:02:04.410
- swimming by and you see like the little,

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:05.790
like the little baby ones.

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:06.623
- [Derek] The baby ones are the best.

00:02:06.623 --> 00:02:07.590
- They were playing around-
- Yeah.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:08.490
- with the older ones.

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:09.323
- [Kelly] That's magical.

00:02:09.323 --> 00:02:12.330
- It was like surreal,
magical. It was crazy.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:15.000
And it was, it felt
like I really understood

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.380
that they were a family.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:17.213
- [Derek] Mm-hmm.

00:02:17.213 --> 00:02:18.900
- It was the strangest experience,

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:20.760
but it was just beautiful.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:22.950
- I mean, you, we don't pause enough.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:26.820
Like that's a moment that not
really anyone's gonna have.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:27.653
- Yeah, no, and, and-

00:02:27.653 --> 00:02:28.486
- Do you know what I'm
saying, how special is that?

00:02:28.486 --> 00:02:29.520
- It was work for me, you know.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:30.666
Like I was I was getting paid to be there.

00:02:30.666 --> 00:02:31.499
- [Derek] Yeah.

00:02:31.499 --> 00:02:33.150
Like I would pay for that experience, but-

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:35.790
- Yeah, but nobody gets
that kind of experience

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:36.623
just out in the wild.

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:37.801
That's like really cool.

00:02:37.801 --> 00:02:38.634
- [Jay] Yeah, it was beautiful.

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:40.330
- I can't imagine the energy off of that.

